    {
      "id": "mechanism",
      "text": "So jewellers melt it with a little copper and silver, which make it hard. In 22 karat, that's just 2 parts in 24. Then a wax copy of the ring is buried in plaster. A hot kiln melts the wax out, leaving a ring-shaped hole. Molten gold is poured in and sets in that exact shape.",
